<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Keshin Dalbhya</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Keshin Darbhya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Keshin Dalbhya was a king of the Panchalas named in late Vedic texts, especially the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmanas">Brahmanas</a>, where he appears as a patron of sacrifice and ritual learning. He is associated with the Keshin clan and with debates over the correct performance of rites. His appearance in these texts is part of the evidence that Panchala, with Kuru, formed a centre of Vedic culture in the Ganges-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> region.</p></div>
